WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.319
Anything a rider, a bike or a browser sends is data. Telo Ride checks it on the way

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:09.902
in, and shows it as text on the way out.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.392
Every request now has a validator. Ids keep the catalogue's shape, power stays

00:00:15.392 --> 00:00:20.045
between zero and two thousand watts, and nothing counts below zero.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.944
Break a rule, or send text where a number belongs, and the answer is 400, validation

00:00:28.944 --> 00:00:33.123
failed, naming the field. No dot-net type name leaks out.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.786
The ride hub refuses the same way: a power reading of minus five watts comes back as

00:00:41.786 --> 00:00:44.172
validation failed, power watts.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.937
A bike whose name holds markup pairs, and its name shows character for character.

00:00:53.937 --> 00:00:55.386
Nothing in it runs.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:07.882
And lint now refuses every way round that: no inner HTML binding, and no bypassing

00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:09.631
Angular's sanitiser.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:14.841
Connect Bike, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
